PageList: count the rows that leave the top of history

Muster numbers a pane's rows for reading them back by line (`muster pane
read`). Counted from the oldest row a screen still holds, a number moves
every time history is pruned to the scrollback limit, so a row number a
reader saved points at other text on the next read. Nothing in the
PageList says how many rows have gone: total_rows only says how many
are left.

This adds PageList.rows_trimmed, which never decreases, counting the rows
that leave the top of the list at the four places that remove them, each
of which already knows how many:

- grow, pruning the first page to stay inside the byte limit;
- Limits.enforce, pruning first pages to stay inside the line limit;
- eraseRows from the start of history (eraseHistory: ED 3, and the
  history half of clearing the screen);
- reset, which discards every row.

A row's index from the oldest row held, plus the count, then numbers it
from the start of the screen's history. A reflow rewraps rows and
eraseActive removes rows below history that remains, and neither is
counted: no single count can renumber what they move.

ghostty_terminal_rows_trimmed, beside Muster's other additions in
src/terminal/c/muster.zig and include/ghostty/vt/muster.h, reads it for
the active screen.

Additive only: one field, one function, no existing behavior changed.
Muster carries this for good rather than sending it upstream. The Zig
test at the end of src/terminal/c/muster.zig covers it.

diff --git a/include/ghostty/vt/muster.h b/include/ghostty/vt/muster.h
index 150eb755..c80dcddc 100644
--- a/include/ghostty/vt/muster.h
+++ b/include/ghostty/vt/muster.h
@@ -107,6 +107,20 @@ GHOSTTY_API GhosttyResult ghostty_terminal_kitty_image_loading_bytes(
 GHOSTTY_API GhosttyResult ghostty_terminal_kitty_image_drop_loading(
     GhosttyTerminal terminal);
 
+/**
+ * How many rows have left the top of the active screen's history since
+ * the screen was made: pruned to the scrollback limit, erased, or
+ * discarded by a reset. A row's index counted from the oldest row held,
+ * plus this, numbers it from the start of the screen's history, which
+ * rows leaving the top do not change. A reflow rewraps rows without
+ * counting them.
+ *
+ * @return GHOSTTY_SUCCESS, or GHOSTTY_INVALID_VALUE for a NULL argument
+ */
+GHOSTTY_API GhosttyResult ghostty_terminal_rows_trimmed(
+    GhosttyTerminal terminal,
+    uint64_t* out);
+
 #ifdef __cplusplus
 }
 #endif
